 observations. Example: Studies and observations of lab results in reference to cholesterol resulted in the interpretation that “all” cholesterol was “bad”. Decades later new studies and observations with better equipment resulted in a different interpretation that there are “two” types of cholesterol “good and bad”. This showed us that we didn’t have all the knowledge to make an accurate interpretation. We interpret what we observe and what we know at our current moment in time. Our interpretations are not necessarily absolute since additional information and knowledge may come at a future time. Man still has very much to learn. So don’t be surprised to find out that Einstein’s Theory of Relativity may not be settled and absolute.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Fri Jan 31 01:15:25 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'display_text_range': [14, 294], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 0, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd Science is something that is usually not settled. Science is based on what man observes and how man interprets those observations. Example: Studies and observations of lab results in reference to cholesterol resulted in the interpretation that “all” cholesterol was “bad”. Decades', 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1885020473618055460', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 1, 'retweet_count': 0, 'retweeted': False, 'user_id_str': '1865141731609710593', 'id_str': '1885134760713859351'}}, '_legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Fri Jan 31 01:15:25 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1